<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelnhausen Privilege</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1186">1186</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gelnhausen Privilege was a charter issued by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> at Gelnhausen in 1186 confirming the rights of the citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a>. It limited the archbishop's power over them and recognised that a serf who lived in the city for a year and a day without being claimed became free. It is regarded as the founding charter of Bremen's civic liberties.</p></div>
